   "text": {
    "L1": "One kilogram equals 1,000 grams. To convert kilograms to grams, multiply by 1,000.",
    "L2": "A common mistake is thinking 50 grams is half a kilogram. Half a kilogram is 500 grams, so that belief is not true.",
    "L3": "For mixed units, change the kilograms to grams first. Then add the extra grams.",
    "L4": "So 2 kilograms becomes 2,000 grams. Add 50 grams to get 2,050 grams.",
    "L5": "Zeros hold empty places. That is why 5 kilograms 8 grams becomes 5,008 grams.",
    "L6": "In the worked example, 650 grams plus 480 grams makes 1,130 grams. Regroup that as 1 kilogram 130 grams.",
    "L7": "Add the kilograms: 2 plus 1 plus 1 makes 4 kilograms. The total is 4 kilograms 130 grams, or 4,130 grams.",
    "L8": "Compare weights only after using the same unit. Since 1 kilogram is 1,000 grams, 900 grams is lighter.",
    "L9": "Now tap the correct conversion for 2 kilograms 50 grams."
   },
